# E2E Testing

## Test Structure

E2E tests live in `cypress/e2e/` by feature:

- `auth/` — login, logout, signup, forgot-password, reset-password
- `athlete/` — feed, create-log, filters, edit-delete-log
- `coach/` — feed, review-status, announcement, filters
- `group/` — group management
- `attendance/` — attendance page
- `account/` — account settings
- `shared/` — protected routes (unauthenticated redirect)
- `mobile/` — viewport-specific behaviour
- `edge-cases/` — misc edge cases

See `cypress/README.md` for setup and structure.

## Adding or Updating Tests

When adding or changing user-facing flows (pages, components, API contracts), add or update Cypress specs in the relevant folder.

- Use `cy.session()` for login caching; credentials from `cypress.env.json`
- Run `pnpm seed:test` to create test users if needed

## Running Tests

After changes that affect user flows, run e2e tests for the modified area:

- Full suite: `pnpm cy:run`
- Specific area: `pnpm cy:run --spec "cypress/e2e/<area>/**/*.cy.ts"`
- Dev server must be running (`pnpm dev`) before running tests
